Package: zypper-declarative
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Declarative convergence of SUSE system state in a snapshot transaction
 zypper-declarative converges a SUSE system to a declarative manifest
 describing the declarable subset of the SUSE Machinery system description
 (packages, repositories, services, and /etc config files), inside a single
 snapshot transaction. The manifest is JSON (Machinery format_version 1) by
 default, with YAML as an opt-in serialisation. It reads the live system into
 the same model itself, so no separate collector is required, and is surfaced
 as a zypper subcommand as well as invokable directly.
